@theme burnout
// Writer-commons, themes batch. From content/arcs/outlines.md, "The struggle themes". Any department, either shift.
// Fill-ins assumed: {home} a place ("Lisk"), {family} with "my" ("my gran"), {hobby} an activity ("painting"),
// {since} a length of time ("five years"). A beat that names one lists it in needs:, so people without it skip it.

== beat 1
tone: light
duty: true
hint: Still here. Yes, still. Just finishing this one. And the next one.
mem: late
them: Me? Still here. Just finishing up. It's only an hour past. Two.   [laugh]
them: Someone's got to. And I'm here anyway. So.
? choice
* Go home. I'll tell the work you said goodnight.   flavour:cheer mem:shooed
  them: Ha. The work doesn't care. Fine. Ten more minutes.
* Can I help you finish?   flavour:practical mem:helped
  them: Would you? Then we'd both be here late. That's worse. That's nicer. I don't know.
them: Ten minutes. Then I'll go. Probably.

== beat 2
tone: heartfelt
hint: Can I sit down? Just for a minute. I haven't sat down all day.
mem: tired
them: Someone asked me to cover their shift. I said yes. I always say yes. That's three this week.   [sigh]
them: I can't say no. If I say no, someone's let down. If I say yes, it's only me let down.
them: I'm so tired. I didn't notice until I sat down just now.
? choice
* Saying no isn't letting them down. It's looking after yourself.   flavour:listen mem:no
  them: Is it? Nobody ever said it like that. Say it again so I remember.
  + them: Say that again. Slowly. I'm going to write it on my hand. I mean it.
* Take a day off. I'll cover your small jobs.   flavour:practical mem:cover
  them: You'd do that? For me? ...Yes. Yes, I think I'll let you.
* You could talk to Oduya. That's what the Counsellor's for.   flavour:share mem:oduya
  them: Oduya. Yes. Maybe. That's not a no. That's a maybe. That's progress.
them: Thanks. I'm going to sit here a bit longer. Just sit. It's nice.

== beat 3
tone: resolution
hint: Guess what I did yesterday? Nothing. Absolutely nothing. It was wonderful.
mem: dayoff
them: I took a day off. A whole one. I slept, I read, I stared at a wall. A good wall.   [laugh]
them: And I said no. Twice this week. Nicely. Nobody minded. Nobody minded!
them: The ship didn't fall apart. Turns out it doesn't need me every minute. Just most of them.
? choice
* Proud of you.   flavour:cheer
  them: Don't. I'll cry. A small cry. A proud one.
  + them: Don't. You'll set me off. Thank you. You saw it before I did.
* How do you feel?   flavour:listen mem:feel
  them: Like myself again. I'd forgotten what that felt like.
them: Same time next week? I'll be off. Look at me. Off.
